  "question": {
    "text": "$N$ divisions on the main scale of a vernier calliper coincide with $(N+1)$ divisions of the vernier scale. If each division of main scale is ' $a$ ' units, then the least count of the instrument is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ZUSp4",
      "text": "\n$a$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "yU3IS",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{a}{N}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qq1Vv",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{N}{N+1} \\times a$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jgrVS",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{a}{N+1}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "No of divisions on main scale $=N$\nNo of divisions on vernier scale $=N+1$ size of main scale division $=a$\nLet size of vernier scale division be $b$ then we have\n$$\na N=b(N+1) \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{b}=\\frac{a N}{N+1}\n$$\nLeast count is $\\mathrm{a}-\\mathrm{b}=\\mathrm{a}-\\frac{a N}{N+1}$ $=a\\left[\\frac{N+1-N}{N+1}\\right]=\\frac{a}{N+1}$",
    "image": null
  },
